/*!

*\page can_get	CAN Get
*
* This instruction reads data from a CAN device. You might need to put the instruction in a loop to make sure that data is read correctly from the CAN device.<BR>
* - The returned result is 1 when the data is received successfully.<br>
* - The returned result is 0 when the data is not received successfully.<br>
*<span style='color:blue'><em><H4> Syntax: </H4></em></span>
*<B>  can_get PinName1, PinName2, FREQ, CANID, VARIABLE;</B><BR>
* - <b>PinName1:</b> CANRD pin name<br>
* - <b>PinName2:</b> CANTD pin name<br>
* - <b>FREQ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; :</b> CAN Bus frequency<br>
* - <b>CANID &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; :</b> CAN ID. This represents the CAN device ID<br>
* - <b>VARIABLE_NAME:</b> A Variable name is required. The results will be saved in this variable (might be an array of int). 
*
* <span style='color:blue'><em><B> Example:</B> </em> </span><br>
*while(1)<br>
*&nbsp;{<br>
*&nbsp;can_get  pb_8, pb_9, 100000,0x10,result;<br>
*&nbsp;if (result!=0){<br>
*&nbsp;&nbsp; print result;<br>
*&nbsp;	}<br>
*&nbsp; delay 100,msec;<br>
*}
*
*
*/
